  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S022",
      "patient_response": "Well, I came in because... I guess I've been doing some things at work and school lately that just don't really make sense. I work as a bookkeeping clerk, you know, mostly dealing with receipts and ledgers for this local hardware store. The store is actually right next to this amazing bakery, and they make these incredible sourdough loaves. I tried baking sourdough a couple of years ago, but my starter died after a week because my apartment is just way too drafty. The landlord refuses to fix the weather stripping on the windows. \n\nBut anyway, at work... I've started doing this thing where I line up all the receipts across the floor. The floor there is that cheap linoleum, the kind that tries to look like real hardwood but you can tell it's fake because the grain pattern repeats every three tiles. I noticed that on my first day there. But yeah, I line the receipts up all over it, or I'll catch myself just tapping the calculator in sets of nine. Just tapping it nine times. \n\nOr... sometimes I'll just go over to the copier and stand there with my hands held up in the air. The copier is a Brother model, it can actually print in color but my boss only ever buys black toner because the color cartridges are a total rip-off. But I'll just stand by it with my hands up until someone finally walks by and asks if I'm okay. I don't really know why I'm doing it, to be honest.",
