    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you find yourself standing with your hands in the air or tapping in sets of nine, what is going through your mind?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, when I'm standing there or doing the tapping... I know it sounds strange, but my mind is just racing with the numbers from work. I get completely convinced that certain invoice totals, or the account numbers, and even the due dates on the accounts are actually messages about me. \n\nWhich reminds me, my own electric bill is always due on the 14th. It's so annoying because I get paid on the 15th, so I'm always technically a day late if I don't plan ahead. I tried calling the utility company once to change the billing cycle, but their hold music is this terrible synth jazz. It sounds exactly like this cheap Casio keyboard I had when I was eight. I used to play the little demo track on it over and over until my mom finally hid the batteries from me. \n\nBut yeah, at the hardware store... even when my supervisor sits down with me and goes over the ledgers—his name is Dave, and he always wears these really bright Hawaiian shirts on Fridays, even when it's literally snowing outside, which is just bizarre—but even when he shows me the screen and proves that they are completely normal entries, I still can't shake it. I still feel like they are tracking whether I understand the pattern. Like the numbers are testing me or something.",
