    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you ever hear voices, sounds, or whispering that other people don't seem to hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, I actually do. Sometimes when I'm just sitting alone at my desk, or, you know, walking home from my classes... I'll hear this man's voice. He says things like, \"check line seven\" or \"you missed the sign.\" It's so clear that I actually stop and look around, but there's literally no one there. \n\nIt kind of freaks me out, especially when I'm walking home. The route I take from campus goes past this really old cemetery. It's got these massive oak trees that drop acorns everywhere in the fall, and they make this loud crunching sound when you step on them. I used to collect acorns when I was a kid because my grandpa told me you could make flour out of them. He grew up on a farm in Ohio and knew all these weird survival tricks. He actually built his own tractor from scratch once. It was painted this bright, cherry red, almost like a fire engine. I always wanted to ride on it, but my mom said it was too dangerous because it didn't have seatbelts. \n\nBut yeah, the voice... it just happens when I'm alone, and it sounds like a real person standing right next to me.",
